-- title:
--   Degree p of κ(̄ j) over κ(̄ j^{ p})
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa$ be a field of characteristic $p$, where $p$ is a prime, and work inside the field $\kappa((q))$ of Laurent series over $\kappa$. Let $\bar j = \mathrm{ModularCurve.jqModC}\,\kappa$ be the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the image under $\kappa$-coefficient reduction (along $\mathbb{Z} \to \kappa$) of the integral power series $\mathrm{ModularCurve.jNum} = E_4^3 \cdot (\text{inverse Dedekind eta unit})$, viewed as a Laurent series; thus $\bar j$ is the mod-$p$ $j$-series. The assertion is that the relative finite rank, in the sense of `IntermediateField.relfinrank`, of the intermediate field $\kappa(\bar j^{\,p})$ generated over $\kappa$ by the single element $\bar j^{\,p}$ inside the intermediate field $\kappa(\bar j)$ generated over $\kappa$ by $\bar j$, equals $p$. Since $\kappa(\bar j^{\,p}) \subseteq \kappa(\bar j)$, this relative rank is the degree $[\kappa(\bar j) : \kappa(\bar j^{\,p})]$.
--
--   This is the statement that Frobenius on the rational function field $\kappa(\bar j)$ has inseparable degree $p$, in the concrete realisation of that function field as the subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by the mod-$p$ $j$-series. It feeds the local analysis of valuation subrings, uniformisers and Gauss reductions on the characteristic-$p$ models of $X_0(p)$, $X_1(p)$ and $X_1(\Gamma_0(p))$-type curves, where the degree-$p$ Frobenius branch has to be counted.
